{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"options":{"content":"","images":{},"widgets":{}},"periodicTable":false,"type":"multiple"},"hints":[{"content":"###Background \n\nThe imaginary unit $\\maroonD{i}$ is defined as $\\sqrt{-1}$. So for any negative real number $-a$, we can express $\\sqrt{-a}$ as $\\maroonD{i}\\sqrt{a}$. ","images":{},"widgets":{}},{"content":"###Converting the Expression \n\n\u003e$\\begin{align}\\pm\\sqrt{-35}\u0026=\\pm\\sqrt{-1\\cdot35}\n\\\\\\\\\u0026=\\pm\\sqrt{-1}\\cdot\\sqrt{35}\n\\\\\\\\\u0026=\\pm\\maroonD{i}\\cdot\\sqrt{35}\n\\\\\\\\\u0026=\\pm\\sqrt{35}\\maroonD{i}\\end{align}$","images":{},"widgets":{}},{"content":"###Summary \n\n- $\\pm\\sqrt{-35}=\\pm\\sqrt{35}\\maroonD{i}$","images":{},"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"**Express the radical using the imaginary unit, $i$.**  \n*Express your answer in simplified form.*\n\n$\\pm\\sqrt{-35}=\\pm$  [[☃ expression 1]]\n\n","images":{},"widgets":{"expression 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answerForms":[{"considered":"correct","form":true,"key":0,"simplify":false,"value":"\\sqrt{35}i"}],"buttonSets":["basic","prealgebra"],"functions":["f","g","h"],"times":false},"static":false,"type":"expression","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
